window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>Ellie Redford's life is pretty much perfect: a fantastic husband, loyal friends, and a steady job at a food magazine. But everyone around her insists there's one thing missing: a baby.</p> <p>While her husband Pete is ready to become a dad, Ellie's not so sure. Babies mean sacrificing late nights, lazy Sundays, and her career ambitions. When she joins a baking class to distract herself, she meets Joe, handsome, charming, and a master of the whisk.</p> <p>What starts as harmless flirting soon turns complicated and Ellie must figure out where her heart truly lies, proving that, unlike baking, there's no perfect recipe for life …</p> <p>A funny, feel-good novel about baking, love, and the unpredictable joys of life—perfect for fans of Lucy Diamond, Laura Jane Williams, and Mhairi McFarlane.</p> <p>Poppy Dolan lives in Berkshire with her husband, where she is a keen baker and crafter as well as a prolific author of many laugh-out-loud romantic comedies.</p>"; 
